  "title": "Kʼinich Janaabʼ Pakal (Pakal the Great) of Palenque",
  "summary": "Kʼinich Janaabʼ Pakal ruled the Maya city of Palenque from 615 CE, when he took the throne at age twelve, until his death in 683 at about eighty. He was buried in the Temple of the Inscriptions, built as his tomb, which later became among the best known Maya monuments.",
